From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: align host-visible blob placement to blob_alignment

Linux 7.2 (commits 7b5121c3374e, 47248e0d8264, 6bd7e82e2653) added
VIRTIO_GPU_F_BLOB_ALIGNMENT and rejects blob sizes that are not a multiple of
blob_alignment, but virtio_gpu_vram_map() still places the node in
host_visible_mm with drm_mm_insert_node(), i.e. without any alignment. The
offset passed in RESOURCE_MAP_BLOB is therefore only guaranteed to be aligned
as long as every node ever inserted had an aligned size. Make the placement
honour blob_alignment explicitly so the host (libkrun on macOS, which maps the
blob with hv_vm_map() at 16K granularity) always gets an aligned offset.

Equivalent in intent to libkrunfw 0023-virtgpu-mixed-page-size.patch, but driven
by the negotiated blob_alignment instead of a hard-coded 64K.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
@@ -160,8 +160,18 @@ static int virtio_gpu_vram_map(struct virtio_gpu_object *bo)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	spin_lock(&vgdev->host_visible_lock);
-	ret = drm_mm_insert_node(&vgdev->host_visible_mm, &vram->vram_node,
-				 bo->base.base.size);
+	/*
+	 * The host maps every blob into the host-visible region at the node
+	 * offset. Hosts with larger pages (16K on Apple silicon) need that
+	 * offset aligned to blob_alignment, not only the size. The region
+	 * base is itself host-page aligned, so aligning the absolute address
+	 * aligns the offset.
+	 */
+	ret = drm_mm_insert_node_generic(&vgdev->host_visible_mm,
+					 &vram->vram_node, bo->base.base.size,
+					 vgdev->has_blob_alignment ?
+					 vgdev->blob_alignment : 0,
+					 0, DRM_MM_INSERT_BEST);
 	spin_unlock(&vgdev->host_visible_lock);
 
 	if (ret)
